WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.753
A crafted PGP

00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:02.826
key can crash

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:04.029
most mail clients

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:05.969
GnuPG has shipped

00:00:05.781 --> 00:00:08.056
GPGME 2.3.1 to

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:08.858
fix a critical

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.188
bug

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.941
tracked as CVE-2026-129975

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.695
An OpenPGP key

00:00:15.554 --> 00:00:16.320
with a very

00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:17.228
long user ID

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.829
can trigger a

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:18.490
double free

00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:19.784
The bug can

00:00:19.596 --> 00:00:20.161
be used to

00:00:19.973 --> 00:00:20.892
leak data from

00:00:20.704 --> 00:00:21.258
apps

00:00:21.294 --> 00:00:22.272
for example by

00:00:22.084 --> 00:00:23.298
sending signed data

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:24.253
and remote code

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:25.314
execution can't be

00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:25.904
ruled out

00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:27.764
GPGME sits inside

00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:29.014
Gpg4win

00:00:29.204 --> 00:00:30.406
most mail clients

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.373
and many chat

00:00:31.185 --> 00:00:31.904
clients

00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:33.428
The root cause

00:00:33.252 --> 00:00:34.348
is a reallocated

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.600
1024-byte buffer whose

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:37.638
new pointer is

00:00:37.497 --> 00:00:38.463
only saved at

00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:38.829
the end of

00:00:38.641 --> 00:00:39.430
a function

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.784
An early return

00:00:40.596 --> 00:00:41.444
leaves a stale

00:00:41.256 --> 00:00:42.270
pointer that gets

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:43.036
freed twice

00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:44.580
Full story on

00:00:44.391 --> 00:00:45.287
the dashboard
